# Rust / Tauri
desktop/src-tauri/target/
desktop/src-tauri/gen/schemas/

# Generated: the desktop frontend is a copy of index.html, made at build time
desktop/dist/

# Node
node_modules/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Generated by desktop/make-icon.mjs
desktop/src-tauri/icons/

# Marketing site is deployed separately, not part of the app repo.
#
# Written as site/* rather than site/ on purpose. Excluding the directory stops
# git from ever looking inside it, and a negation cannot re-include a file whose
# parent is excluded, so the two server config files below would have been
# unreachable. Excluding the contents instead leaves them re-includable.
site/*

# Exceptions: the small hand-written files that configure the server rather
# than make up the site. Nothing else holds a copy of these.
#
# .htaccess carries the CSP, the cache rules and the installer MIME types that
# keep the download mirror usable at all, and it is not part of the routine
# deploy, so it can sit unchanged on the server for months. The IndexNow key
# only proves control of the domain and is public by design; it is served at the
# site root and search engines refuse submissions without it. robots.txt and
# sitemap.xml are edited by hand and shape what search engines do with the site.
#
# The pages themselves stay out. They are large, they change with every release,
# and site/app/index.html is a copy of the app that is already tracked at the
# repo root, so tracking it would mean two copies of a 380 KB file per commit.
!site/.htaccess
!site/20116a2b48a4e637b95b39fe685d433a.txt
!site/robots.txt
!site/sitemap.xml
